  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday Night through Saturday)\nIssued at 1134 PM CDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nConvection is likely to be trending down Sunday evening with loss\nof daytime instability. The front will continue to push westward \nSunday night into Monday with drier and slightly cooler air \nfiltering in from the east behind it. CAMs indicate isolated \nshowers and storms will again be possible to the west of the \nboundary Monday afternoon, but with ridging intensifying overhead,\ncoverage is more uncertain. Based on HREF/REFS guidance, have \nintroduced 15 percent PoPs for parts of E OK Monday afternoon. \nHigh temperatures will remain near or above 100 degrees Monday \nwith heat headlines probable for parts of the area again.\n\nThe center of the ridge moves directly overhead Tuesday into \nWednesday with more hot and dry conditions. Heat headlines will \nlikely be required through this period. By Wednesday night, the \nridge is expected to flatten as a strong upper level low develops \nacross the Upper Midwest into Canada. This is will force a cold \nfront south into our vicinity with increasing rain and storm \npotential. The front will be weaker by the time it reaches our \narea, and there is still uncertainty how far south it will make \nit, but it should provide some cooler temperatures and increased \nrain potential for at least northern portions of the CWA Thursday \ninto Friday. Southerly flow and above average temperatures return \nto the area ahead of a stronger cold front which may push into the\narea late next weekend.",
